# .trivyignore — Trivy CVE suppression list
#
# FORMAT (one entry per line):
#   CVE-YYYY-NNNNN  # exp:YYYY-MM-DD; <justification referencing the US/control that mitigates>
#
# RULES (enforced by scripts/ci/check_trivy_results.py in the trivy-scan job):
#   1. Every active entry (non-blank, non-comment-only line) MUST have an
#      exp:YYYY-MM-DD tag.  Entries without an expiry fail the build.
#   2. Maximum suppression window is 90 days from the date of addition.
#   3. Expired entries fail the build — they must be reviewed, extended (if
#      the upstream fix is still unavailable), or removed.
#   4. Each entry MUST reference a justification (e.g. "no fix upstream;
#      mitigated by <control>" or "false-positive; <reason>").
#
# ADDING A NEW SUPPRESSION:
#   CVE-YYYY-NNNNN  # exp:YYYY-MM-DD; <justification>
#
# Example (replace with real CVEs as they arise):
#   CVE-2024-00001  # exp:2026-10-01; no upstream fix available; mitigated by US-048 mTLS network isolation
#
# Currently no active suppressions.
